A||N||7||polomeno||Any tips before changing head gasket?||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||05-16-2001||06:13 PM||||Hey guys, I have a 84 , 4 cylinder 2.5 and need to change the head gasket.... have everything i need, new bolts, gasket, head checked and machined, anything i should know or any tips? My old head has gasket used on it? should this be used cause old head bolt broke... any help is appreciated<P>thanks<P>John<P>P.S. also i'd like to thank bubbajoxx for providing a replacement head right away.. good guy !||||reg||1
Z||000001||polomeno||05-16-2001||07:23 PM||||anyone??||||reg||1
Z||000002||spideyfoot||05-16-2001||07:45 PM||||Spray every bolt you can see with PS Blaster. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||spideyfoot||05-16-2001||07:49 PM||||Spray every bolt you see with PS Blaster. Let soak spray again. Go ahead and bust a knuckle open so you can get it out of the way. I found somme good step by steps when I searched head removal or something like that. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||05-16-2001||08:11 PM||||Maybe you have already seen this:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009419.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009419.html</A> <P>Good luck!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||05-16-2001||08:27 PM||||What is ps blaster and where can I get it?||||reg||5
Z||000006||PBJ||05-16-2001||08:32 PM||||I would recommend you replace the valve seals. there is updated ones for exhaust-more than just the o ring.  Umbrella type. suppose to cure smoke during or after prolonged idle.||||reg||1
